From f567a069d3d47ecebce36a6e3de1a999b5f9c039 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Otavio Salvador <otavio@ossystems.com.br>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 03:24:14 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 13/13] feat: choose the flake dev shell a project's direnv
 environment loads

Flakes often define several dev shells, and the one a project's .envrc names is not always the one
the agent needs. Editing the .envrc would change the user's own terminal too.

A project setting now picks the shell. T3 Code lists the flake's devShells for the current system
and runs direnv with a wrapper config that loads the user's direnv setup, then points use flake at
the chosen shell. That shell caches its profile in its own layout directory, because nix-direnv
deletes the other profiles beside the one it writes, which would evict the terminal's shell. The
thread details panel shows the shell, and a changed choice reloads the environment on the next
message.
